(F) t2(A), m = 4 (one error cell of 16, d = 10, p = 1/16): extra length of the single-cell rule memoriser over
    the good model's rate code, and the secants that decide whether the good model is a vertex
  prover's code: rule memoriser minus good model = 4 bits (with exact ceiling); mine: 5 bits; the rule is longer, not cheaper
  prover's code: model secant (coin -> good) = 45.24, rule secant (good -> rule) = 86.35: the good model is not a vertex because the rule's secant is larger
